+# Demo clarity and reliability — 24 October 2026
+
+## Starting point
+
+Recovered canonical and remote integration HEAD: f75af1ac22a7260487556fc9231f4e290489c2e0. Published and running application: b20685d1670b33b941b1bfcb902638a879c01b93 (Sites v48). Both existing local workspaces are healthy. Work proceeds in the isolated codex/casepath-demo-polish-20261024 normal clone.
+
+## Bounded outcome
+
+1. Open the public presentation on a consistent, immediate introduction. Avoid rendering an unrelated case during preparation. Keep all recorded-history verification and explicit failure handling. Start playback only when its admitted histories are ready.
+2. Make the receiving-case reuse result legible within the reference viewport: selected process step, actual historical before/after, receiving-case source passages, exact saved version and current effect. Keep historical effects distinct from current evaluation; show the whole process when requested.
+3. Verify the actual user journey at desktop and mobile sizes, source fidelity, reduced motion, read-only public behavior, exact-version pinning and evidence visibility. Capture a new continuous public film and fresh viewer assessment after deployment.
+
+## North-star self-review before editing
+
+- Read AGENTS.md, NORTHSTAR.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and active HYBRID_DEVELOPMENT.md.
+- Use the approved white/Mulish/crimson canvas, 75px top bar, source rail and five review roles.
+- Preserve original sources, source bounds and the source → fact → process relationship.
+- Derive each result from actual accepted events and current evaluation; no invented role actions or effect.
+- Engineering actor remains Test handler. Qualified approval is pending. No claim outcome is authorised by these edits.
+- Keep the existing public recorded histories and their original provider usage unchanged. No model or external-facts calls.
+- Preserve the active 4173 and 4194 servers and all existing data. Preview in an owned separate port and disposable QA copy.
+- Root integrates disjoint worker edits, updates asset hashes, seals the complete source, runs the mandatory gate and deploys matching Site/API identities only after verification.
+
+## Acceptance evidence to produce
+
+- Measured cold-entry behavior and honest slow/failure state.
+- Focused bootstrap and review regression results.
+- Original-source and exact-version real-browser assertions, full-page desktop/mobile screenshots.
+- Reference side-by-side / overlay / difference review with explicit justified deviations.
+- Completed full-gate terminal receipt for the sealed source.
+- Deployed matching identities, read-only case walkthrough, continuous film and independent fresh frame review.
+
+The previous release remains available while this candidate is developed. This plan is not a completion or qualification claim.
+
+## Development environment
+
+The launcher correctly rejected a linked worktree because its Git source authority must be a real directory. Development moved to this ordinary clone; the unchanged source guard is retained. The abandoned worktree has no product edits.
+
+## Pre-seal implementation and review
+
+The candidate now presents a case-neutral explanation immediately and never paints the unrelated first roster case before showcase admission. The eight independent state reads run together while the existing state, source, operation-chain and checkpoint admission checks remain in place. Owned reads are cancelled on navigation; late replies cannot start playback. Hidden-page admission waits, and invalid data exposes an honest retry.
+
+Preparation and failure status, including the entire retry control, are visible beside the walkthrough title at 1440 × 900 and 375 × 812. The shared purpose and admitted introduction retain their position and copy. The mobile failure page intentionally scrolls for the remaining explanatory content; recovery controls are visible before that content. Details is separated from the error sentence.
+
+The receiving-case Result view now leads with the affected step and the recorded before/after. Its three evidence cards, qualification note and actual next action are fully visible at the reference desktop viewport. The full twelve-step process remains available through a keyboard-accessible disclosure; editing and preview states keep the full graph. The affected-step marker copies the rendered process marker, including after selection, disclosure changes and reload. Earlier process connections are explicitly retained only when recorded graph evidence supports that statement.
+
+Historical reuse and current evaluation remain distinct. Both historical states were already waiting. The protective next action remains “Preserve challenge or extension deadline.” The later case keeps its own original source passages (30. Juni / 31. Juli), facts and reviews. It pins exact version 1 even after version 2 is published. “Saved by Test handler” remains engineering provenance, and qualified review remains required.
+
+### Completed focused verification
+
+- 13 opening/recorded-admission unit regressions.
+- 6 actual presentation browser scenarios, including the complete six-act presentation, delayed reads, all eight out-of-order responses, navigation cancellation, invalid identity and hidden-tab admission.
+- 19 review consequence unit regressions.
+- One complete isolated deterministic browser journey through original source review, actual correction, exact version save, preview, acceptance, later-case application, reload/version pinning, disclosure and keyboard inspection, and mobile/reduced-motion behavior.
+- The 19 opening checks were rerun after the final visibility-only adjustment. They and the five actual opening screenshots passed.
+- Root visually inspected the final desktop/mobile preparation and failure frames, admitted introduction, and receiving-case result/source reader. No unresolved layout blocker remains in the changed screens.
+- Independent source review found no concrete blocker in the startup admission/cancellation implementation or the final payoff marker/retention delta. Root reviewed the final rail-only markup/CSS adjustment and its actual browser evidence.
+
+The complete official gate, public deployment identity/asset checks, 300 primary read soak, final protected-data/usage readback, fresh continuous film review and all three concept comparisons remain mandatory after this seal. This pre-seal review does not claim those future stages are complete.
+
+### Deliberate design decisions
+
+The neutral loading view reserves the admitted introduction's desktop position rather than inventing case content. It shows a concise textual preparation state without cosmetic progress claims. The accepted reuse result prioritizes the actual change, while the complete process remains one disclosure away. Original documents remain accessible through the existing source reader and zoom control. The result does not imply a newly unblocked decision or qualified approval.
+
+Existing 4173 and 4194 services remain available during development. Any final promotion of the owned engineering service must retain its actual data directory, compare journal hashes/counts before and after startup, and perform no seed replay or provider work.
